title: Amarjeet_Day1
tags: 
position: -7,-175
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Spiritual_1>>
<<SetBGSprite ShivTemple>>

After a particularly frustrating cricket practice where his shots lacked consistency and his focus kept wandering, Raju chooses to visit the small neighborhood temple where Amarjeet, the elderly priest, has always offered quiet wisdom.

The evening shadows lengthen across the temple courtyard. The familiar scent of incense mingles with distant neighborhood sounds. Raju's footsteps slow as he approaches, his cricket bat feeling heavy—weighed down by accumulated frustrations.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: Ah, young one. You come with dust on your face and a bat in your hand.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: But I can see something troubling you. Your practice didn't go well today, did it?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Surprised">>
Raju feels surprised by the priest's perceptiveness. He had hoped his frustration wasn't so obvious.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: Baba, I don't understand. Some days I hit every ball perfectly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Sad">>
Raju: Other days, I can't connect with anything. I practice the same way, but results keep changing.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Am I doing something wrong?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: Tell me, beta. What do you think discipline means?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: Most young people think they understand this word. But few grasp its deeper significance.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: To follow rules? To practice regularly?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: I try to do both of those things with my cricket.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: Rules and practice—yes, those are the surface of discipline.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: But deeper than that, true discipline is focus. It is keeping your mind steady regardless of circumstances.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: See this diya, child? The wind pushes against it, trying to extinguish the flame.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: Yet the light survives because it has found steadiness.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: So too must your mind be if you want consistency in cricket.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: So when my shots are inconsistent, it's not my practice that's wrong?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: It's because my mind isn't steady like the flame?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Smiling">>
Amarjeet: Exactly, beta. Your hands know the technique. Your body understands the movements.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Smiling">>
Amarjeet: But your mind wanders. True discipline means keeping attention only on this moment.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Smiling">>
Amarjeet: This shot. This breath.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: I think I understand, Baba.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: But achieving that kind of focus... it's not easy, is it?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: Nothing worth achieving is easy, child.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: If you truly wish to learn this deeper discipline, return tomorrow evening.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: We will continue this conversation.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: Thank you, Baba. I will come back.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I want to learn this kind of focus.

<<HideCharacter>>
As Raju walks home, he carries both his bat and a new perspective. Amarjeet has offered something more valuable than cricket technique—insight into the mental foundations that support all achievement.

<<set $Amarjeet_Day = 2>>
<<EndEvent true>>
===

title: Amarjeet_Day2
tags: 
position: -7,-75
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Spiritual_1>>
<<SetBGSprite ShivTemple>>

True to his promise, Raju returns to the temple the following evening, determined to learn more about mental discipline.

The temple courtyard glows softly in evening light. Amarjeet tends to the oil lamps with steady devotion. When he sees Raju approaching, his expression shows pleased surprise.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Smiling">>
Amarjeet: So, you came back, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Smiling">>
Amarjeet: Few boys your age keep promises, especially when teaching involves hard work.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju feels both pride in keeping his commitment and nervous anticipation. Has he understood yesterday's lessons correctly?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: Baba, I've been thinking about what you said. About mental steadiness.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: I tried to focus only on each individual ball during today's practice.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: It felt... different. Better, but also more difficult than I expected.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: You've discovered something important, beta.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: Discipline transforms the quality of both success and failure.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Smiling">>
Amarjeet: When your mind is steady, even errors become teachers.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: But tell me this. Was it easy to maintain that focus?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: Did your mind want to wander to other thoughts?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: No, Baba, it wasn't easy at all.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Serious">>
Raju: My mind kept wanting to think about other things.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Quizzical">>
Raju: Keeping attention on just the current moment felt like... like holding water in cupped hands.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Smiling">>
Amarjeet: A perfect analogy, beta!

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: Mental discipline is indeed like holding water. It requires constant, gentle attention.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: The skill is in finding the right amount of focused care.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: So how do I get better at this holding, Baba?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Raju" "Excited">>
Raju: How do I make my focus stronger and more consistent?

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: That is a question that requires time to answer properly.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Neutral">>
Amarjeet: Come back tomorrow, child.

<<SetCharacterExpression "Amarjeet" "Smiling">>
Amarjeet: Tomorrow I will show you different paths to strengthen your mind.

<<HideCharacter>>
As Raju walks home, he feels the satisfaction of a student who has engaged seriously with challenging material. His voluntary return has deepened the priest's investment in his education.

